<title>SRI LANKA: Weather-Showers seen over many parts of Sri Lanka.</title>
<headline>Weather-Showers seen over many parts of Sri Lanka.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka's metereological department released the following rainfall figures for 24 hours ending Thursday morning</p>
<p>Hydro catchment areas (in mm):</p>
<p>    Bowathenna		0</p>
<p>    Canyon		    0</p>
<p>    Castlereigh	     15.4</p>
<p>    Kotmale		   30.5</p>
<p>    Laxapana		  0</p>
<p>    Moussakele		20.3</p>
<p>    Norton		    0</p>
<p>    Randenigala	     0</p>
<p>    Victoria		  1.8</p>
<p>    Samanalawewa	    2.5</p>
<p>    Ukuwela		   0</p>
<p>    Rantembe		  1.3</p>
<p>The department forecast thundershowers at a few places in the Central, Sabaragamuwa, North Central and Uva provinces in the afternoon or evening. Isolated showers wil prevail in the Western province and in the Galle and Matara districts, it said.</p>
</text>
